                <pb facs="0772" n="682" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg682"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.9411/34: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-07T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 7,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received June 7—9:32
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>900. Your May 10, noon, and May 24, 7 p.m. The chance has been found to convey
                    informally your suggestions in substance to the Foreign Office. I have been
                    given assurance that they will be fully considered and that in any redrafting of
                    the Anglo–Japanese Treaty of Alliance it will be made quite clear that the
                    Alliance is not aimed at the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
